{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>And the name of the daughter of Asher was Serach.</b> Because she is mentioned among those who went out of Egypt, she is mentioned here. And one must wonder what 'and the name' means. And also regarding the Targum one must wonder: ״ושום בת אתת אשר סרח״ — it implies that she was not the daughter of Asher but the daughter of his wife, whom Asher raised, and therefore she is called by his name; and this is the meaning of 'and the name' — Asher had over her only the name, but she was not his daughter. Yet one must wonder: if she bore one of the tribes, why did they not mention him? And if another, of the rest of the world, why is she traced back to Jacob? Perhaps she was indeed the daughter of Asher, and because her name was especially well-known for piety and good deeds, 'and the name' is written about her. But indeed the language of the Targum is forced."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:16.056749373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}